Defensive coding
API design thinking
Production mindset
🧠 NOW — DEEP DIVE
SHALLOW vs DEEP COPY (VERY IMPORTANT)
Google loves this topic.
🔹 SHALLOW COPY (outer only)
What it copies
The container
❌ NOT nested objects
Examples
lst.copy()
lst[:]
copy.copy(lst)
Diagram
Original list ──┐
                ├── inner object (shared)
Copied list  ───┘
When shallow copy is OK
Flat lists
Immutable inner objects
Performance matters
🔹 DEEP COPY (full isolation)
What it copies
Container
All nested objects (recursively)
Example
import copy
new_lst = copy.deepcopy(old_lst)
Proof
lst = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
d = copy.deepcopy(lst)

d[0].append(99)
print(lst)
Output
[[1, 2], [3, 4]]
When deep copy is required
Nested mutable data
Configuration templates
Independent processing
Safety > performance
⭐ Google follow-up question
“Why not always use deep copy?”
Correct answer
“Deep copy is more expensive in terms of memory and performance, so I use it only when full isolation is required.”
